cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MEMBRANE in academic or technical work, please cite this
  software using the metadata in this file.
title: >-
  MEMBRANE: Adaptive KV-Cache Planning for llama.cpp
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Altıntaş
    given-names: Kadir Eren
repository-code: "https://github.com/kadireren7/membrane"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  MEMBRANE is an open-source llama.cpp runtime layer for KV-cache
  precision and CPU/GPU residency planning under constrained memory. It
  plans GPU layer offload, whole-cache Q8/Q5/adaptive KV precision, and
  static CPU/GPU KV residency before generation (an --auto joint
  planner with bounded apply-time fallback), with --plan-only/--doctor/
  --list-devices/--inspect-model diagnostics and machine-readable JSON
  output, on CPU and Vulkan backends. Compressed KV (q8/q5/adaptive) is
  validated for LLM_ARCH_LLAMA and LLM_ARCH_QWEN2 models against real
  local fixtures -- not a claim of universal architecture or hardware
  coverage; see docs/compatibility.md for the current matrix. An
  official Debian-family amd64 .deb package is available; independent
  multi-host validation beyond the maintainer's own development
  hardware remains limited as of this release. This citation targets
  the latest stable release, v0.3.0; the repository's main branch may
  contain development changes beyond it. Archived experiments, negative
  results, and benchmark/FPGA/CXL simulation provenance live in the
  companion repository kadireren7/membrane-research.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - LLM
  - KV cache
  - inference
  - memory management
  - Vulkan
  - quantization
  - GPU offload
